    "turn_idx": 28,
    "turn_text": "well yeah Possibly, we paid a heavy tax liability. My dad was a big farmer. He had several different businesses because his dream was that all four of his kids could stay there and farm if they wanted to. So everybody that knew him knew he worked harder than anybody they knew. He was outside before anybody else woke up and he didn't come in until after everybody else was in bed. So he was a very hard worker. There was a comment made by many reporters that if we had done better, estate planning that we probably wouldn't have had to pay these taxes. And I found that very offensive, extremely offensive. That's the perfect argument for why then this tax needs to be repealed. If only the wealthy rich, really smart people can get out of paying it because they can hire enough attorneys to do the planning to avoid it, then it's hitting everyone else and it proves how unfair it is. So I found that extremely offensive. My dad had done estate planning. He had paid for it. He hadn't gotten to the attorney yet to sign his new will. So he died unexpectedly and the lawyer called us and said, I'm sorry, your dad's new will was done. He just hadn't signed it. So we can't use it. So they the attacks on my family were were shocking to me. What it taught me was how hard some people will fight to keep attacks because a lot of the media, they already had proof. It had been in public record for 24 years that our family paid the death taxes, yet they wrote editorials.",
