    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/6/96369.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 41,
    "turn_text": "Yeah. You know, and overwhelmingly business, agriculture leaders, they want it repealed too. You know, I'm not on an island with this. We have all kinds of organizations that recognize how unfair this tax is. It's, and imagine the situation we're in now. How hard is it to do estate planning? when we have a double exemption for the next eight years and then it goes back down. Families, the uncertainty of now is even more complicated. I'm glad we're protecting a lot of different businesses right now for the next eight years. But I have people coming up to me and say, I guess I have to hope that I die in the next eight years or my kids are going to have to pay these taxes. So that's the thing that I was disappointed in. that we at least couldn't get that exemption level doubled permanently. But unfortunately, that's one of the ramifications of doing tax reform in a budget bill. A budget bill that we had to do it within the ramifications and guidelines of the rules of the Senate. And that made it a much more difficult needle to threat. But we are in a better spot than we were before this discussion started.",
